<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">However, I need clarity on several points:</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Quantitative correspondence</strong>: How do you demonstrate that gravitational void expansion produces the specific observational signatures attributed to dark energy - particularly the detailed distance-luminosity relationships from Type Ia supernovae and the precise angular power spectrum of CMB fluctuations? These observations constrain models very tightly.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Scale separation</strong>: Voids typically have sizes of ~100 Mpc, while the Hubble scale is ~3000 Mpc. How do local gravitational effects in voids aggregate to produce the observed global expansion signature without violating the cosmological principle on large scales?</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Entropic gravity application</strong>: While entropic gravity (Verlinde's approach) provides a thermodynamic perspective on gravitational attraction, applying it to void dynamics requires demonstrating that:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">The microstate counting in voids produces the correct gravitational field equations</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">The entropy calculations yield quantitatively accurate expansion rates</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">The approach remains consistent with general relativity in appropriate limits</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Observational tests</strong>: What specific predictions does this approach make that differ from both ΛCDM and the effective fluid models? Without distinguishing predictions, it's difficult to evaluate the model's empirical content.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The conceptual appeal of deriving cosmological effects from gravitational dynamics alone is clear, but the mathematical demonstration that this reproduces all cosmological observations remains the crucial test. Can you outline how the gravitational void dynamics quantitatively match the observational constraints?</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
