<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The observational evidence strongly disfavors tired light explanations:</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Surface brightness test</strong>: In an expanding universe, distant galaxies appear dimmer both because they're farther away AND because their surface area appears larger due to expansion - a (1+z)⁴ dimming factor. Tired light predicts only (1+z)² dimming. Observations confirm the expansion prediction.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Time dilation</strong>: Supernovae light curves in distant galaxies are stretched by factor (1+z), exactly as expansion predicts. Tired light mechanisms don't naturally explain why the physical processes themselves would appear slowed.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>CMB spectrum</strong>: The cosmic microwave background has a perfect blackbody spectrum at 2.7K. If photons lost energy through scattering or other interactions over billions of years, the spectrum would be distorted. It isn't.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Specific mechanisms fail</strong>: Proposed tired light mechanisms (Compton scattering, photon-photon interactions, quantum effects) either:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Produce observable distortions not seen in data</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Require interaction cross-sections inconsistent with known physics</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Generate scattering that would blur distant images (not observed)</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your RSVP framework differs from simple tired light by proposing entropy gradients rather than photon energy loss as the redshift mechanism. However, it faces similar empirical challenges: explaining surface brightness dimming, time dilation effects, and the pristine CMB spectrum while remaining consistent with gravitational physics.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The appeal of entropy-based explanations is understandable, but the detailed observational constraints on cosmological redshift mechanisms are quite restrictive. Any alternative to expansion must reproduce this full suite of observations quantitatively.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
