d and no where to move energy into except into neighbouring regions. Niel Turok's work shows its not the universe expanding but an expanding scale at which we measure it. When the universe began expanding inflaton field is just a relative expansion of lighter regions compared to heavier regions by the same mechanism. The universe began as a solid brick for 380,000 it was rearranging internally and at recombination hydrogen atoms formed everywhere in the universe at once relaxing into a mist extending everywhere at once. I know it isn't obvious because it's not the way it's currently formulated or described but I don't see any other coherent explanation. What we call Expansion is still just the smoothing out of the universe.</p></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-y-4 bg-bg-100/80 backdrop-blur-sm translate-x-1 group-hover:translate-x-0.5 border-0.5 border-border-300 p-0.5 shadow-sm opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
