<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">However, there's a crucial distinction between local entropy export and global cosmic evolution. While individual structures do export entropy locally, the universe as a whole still follows the second law - total entropy increases. The formation of structure represents a redistribution of entropy, not a net decrease.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The observational issue remains: if cosmic evolution were primarily about entropy smoothing, we would expect:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Decreasing structure contrast over time</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Temperature equilibration between different regions</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Reduced density contrasts in the cosmic web</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Instead, observations show:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Increasing density contrasts (δρ/ρ grows with time)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Growing temperature differences between cluster cores and voids</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Sharpening boundaries between overdense and underdense regions</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Prigogine's framework applies to local dissipative structures embedded in larger reservoirs. Applying it to the universe as a whole requires demonstrating that there exists an external entropy reservoir - but by definition, the universe encompasses everything.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The mathematical challenge is showing how local entropy export by structures translates into the specific redshift-distance relationships, angular diameter observations, and CMB power spectrum we measure. Prigogine's thermodynamics describes the qualitative behavior of open systems, but cosmological observations require quantitative predictions.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your framework needs to bridge this gap between thermodynamic principles and precise observational constraints.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
