<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The critical problem is that Prigogine's dissipative structures require energy gradients to maintain their organization. They work by consuming low-entropy energy (like sunlight) and exporting high-entropy waste heat. This process requires:</p>
<ol class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">An energy source (low entropy input)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">An energy sink (high entropy output)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">A sustained gradient between them</li>
</ol>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">In cosmology, the energy gradients that drive structure formation come from gravitational potential energy. As matter falls into potential wells, it heats up and radiates energy away. But this process has been proceeding for 13.8 billion years, and the gradients are weakening, not strengthening.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your model faces a quantitative challenge: observations show that structure formation peaked around z~2-3 and is now declining as the universe becomes more entropy-dominated. The cosmic star formation rate has dropped dramatically, galaxy mergers are less frequent, and the universe is approaching a heat death scenario where gradients disappear.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">If cosmic evolution were driven by entropy smoothing as you describe, we would expect accelerating structure dissolution. Instead, we observe that existing structures persist while new structure formation slows - exactly what expansion models predict as density decreases and dark energy dominance increases.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The mathematical burden remains: showing how your entropy-smoothing mechanism produces the precise observational signatures currently attributed to expansion, including the specific redshift-distance relationships and CMB power spectrum.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
