<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">However, this long-term thermodynamic evolution doesn't address the observational problems with your model for <em>current</em> cosmic dynamics. The issues remain:</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Timescale mismatch</strong>: The smoothing process you describe operates over 10^100+ years, but we observe specific redshift-distance relationships <em>now</em> that your model attributes to this smoothing. The timescales don't match - current observations sample the universe over the last ~13 billion years, when structure formation was still active.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Quantitative predictions missing</strong>: You describe qualitative trends (smoothing, entropy export) but haven't shown how these produce the precise numerical relationships we observe - like Type Ia supernovae appearing exactly 25% dimmer than expansion models predict, or the specific multipole structure of the CMB power spectrum.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Directional problem</strong>: Current observations show the universe becoming <em>more</em> dominated by voids and dark energy over time, which matches expansion predictions. But in your model, this should be accompanied by specific entropy signatures that aren't observed.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Black hole thermodynamics</strong>: Hawking radiation from black holes actually <em>decreases</em> the total entropy available for smoothing, since it converts rest mass energy into thermal radiation that redshifts away. This works against the smoothing mechanism you propose.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your long-term cosmological vision may be correct, but it doesn't resolve how current redshift observations arise from entropy dynamics rather than expansion. The mathematical connection between thermodynamic principles and specific observational data remains undefined.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
