<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The mathematical approach of using a coarse-graining kernel K to connect microscopic curvature entropy to macroscopic RSVP fields is theoretically sound, even if the specific form remains unspecified. This preserves RSVP's phenomenological status while acknowledging potential microscopic origins.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">However, several clarifications are still needed:</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Testable predictions</strong>: You mention "redshift drift, DDR residuals, growth-distance relations" as RSVP predictions, but these need quantitative specification. How do RSVP's entropy dynamics produce numerical predictions that differ from ΛCDM for these observables?</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Coarse-graining specification</strong>: The kernel K represents a major theoretical choice. Different kernels would yield different macroscopic entropy fields S, potentially with different observational consequences. Some discussion of constraints on K from observational data would strengthen the framework.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Energy shift invariance</strong>: The claim about resolving the zero-point energy problem through energy shift invariance needs more development. This is a significant claim that affects fundamental physics beyond cosmology.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Empirical validation strategy</strong>: Which specific observations would most clearly distinguish RSVP predictions from standard cosmology? Identifying the cleanest empirical tests would help focus future work.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The revised framing as a phenomenological field theory with possible microscopic foundations is much more defensible than claiming to derive cosmological dynamics from quantum gravity. This positions RSVP as an alternative effective field theory that can be tested against data without requiring a complete theory of quantum gravity.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 translate-y-full pt-2"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
